// get_user_id_by_email.dg — resolves a CRM user's numeric record id from their login email.
//
// Needed because zoho.loginuserid returns the user's EMAIL, not their CRM record id, inside a
// Deluge custom function — confirmed via Zoho's own community documentation (there's a
// long-running, unresolved community thread titled almost exactly "zoho.loginuserid does not
// work because it returns the email"; there is no single official built-in for "give me the
// numeric id of whoever is actually invoking this function"). Used by resolve_actor.dg.
//
// zoho.crm.getRecords("users", ...) returns a Map with a "users" key holding the list, not the
// list directly — confirmed live (iterating the raw Map result was silently a no-op).
//
// TODO before first real run: zoho.crm.getRecords("users", ...) is noted in some Zoho reference
// material as available only on Zoho CRM Vertical Solutions editions — confirm this works on
// this org's actual CRM edition; if not, an alternative (a COQL query, or a small
// hand-maintained email->id lookup org variable alongside Digest_active_users) will be needed.
// Also TODO: this only fetches the first 200 active users — loop additional pages if this org
// ever has more than 200 active users.

string standalone.getUserIdByEmail(String email)
{
	users = zoho.crm.getRecords("users", 1, 200, {"type": "ActiveUsers"});
	for each u in users.get("users") {
		if (u.get("email") == email) {
			return u.get("id");
		}
	}
	return null;
}
